  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: php security update",
  "description": "A critical security update for PHP on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Extended Lifecycle Support addresses multiple vulnerabilities including remote code execution, cross-site scripting, memory corruption, buffer overflow, denial of service, information disclosure, and privilege escalation. These issues affect various PHP components such as the SOAP extension, PHP-FPM, PHP-CGI, session handling, and libgd. The update mitigates risks from use-after-free bugs, improper URL sanitation, malformed data processing, and signature bypasses.",
